You are editing a C++17 repository (the workspace root is a git worktree). Do not run git and do not build. Make exactly the change below and nothing else. Never print or log any secret value.

BACKGROUND (credential data-loss bug): in Settings > DigiKey, the "Client secret" row shows a masked value. Selecting it and pressing Enter without typing commits an EMPTY secret as a staged change; pressing Save then overwrites the stored DigiKey secret in the OS credential store with an empty string. The DigiKey setup wizard already rejects an empty secret; the Settings panel does not. We reject an empty secret in the panel the same way the neighbouring Scan port field rejects an invalid port (show a message and stay in the editor; Esc already cancels the edit).

STEPS
1. Open src/ui/pages/settings/SettingsPageState.cpp and find the function that commits a settings field edit (App::commitSettingsFieldEdit). Inside it, find the `SettingsCategory::DigiKey` branch with `switch (settingsField_)` and its `case 1:` which reads:
      case 1:
        stagedDigiKeySecret_ = inputBuffer_;
        stagedDigiKeySecretChanged_ = true;
        break;
2. Replace those four lines with exactly:
      case 1:
        if (trim(inputBuffer_).empty()) {
          setMessage("Client secret cannot be empty; press Esc to keep the stored secret", 4);
          return;
        }
        stagedDigiKeySecret_ = inputBuffer_;
        stagedDigiKeySecretChanged_ = true;
        break;
   (Check that `trim` is used elsewhere in the same function, e.g. `trim(inputBuffer_)` in the other DigiKey cases, so it is already available. The InventatoryScan port branch just above uses the same `setMessage(..., 4); return;` pattern.)
3. Do not touch any other case, file or function. Re-read the edited region and confirm braces balance. Reply with the before/after of the edit.
